<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:47:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How important are Nvidia and Jensen Huang to the US economy?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c68798vdprwpo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:45:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T06:04:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c68798vdprwpo--9194ddb07971.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c68798vdprwpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The former Nvidia chief executive has been at the centre of the artificial intelligence boom.</summary></entry><entry><title>Security flaw found in Java, world's third-largest programming language</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cke89jevqm1vo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:45:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T05:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cke89jevqm1vo--4122aa6872a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cke89jevqm1vo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The same tech start-up that discovered a PHP flaw used AI to uncover a critical software bug in one of the world's most popular computer language programs.</summary></entry><entry><title>Watch: Marco Rubio says recent tech outages are 'completely unrelated' to one another</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cx1l0vm87yl9o#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:47:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T05:10:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cx1l0vm87yl9o--f9f859c42f15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cx1l0vm87yl9o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Microsoft, major US banks, Apple and Air Traffic authorities have been hit over recent days by tech glitches.</summary></entry><entry><title>Waymo pulls driverless taxis from all US freeways</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmy86pp336qlo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:45:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T03:07:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmy86pp336qlo--ccc4389da68a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmy86pp336qlo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The decision comes after California banned Waymo's driverless vehicles from operating on the state's highways following a series of traffic incidents.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia says it won't reinstate Huang as it reports soaring sales</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm2kl50vkwkdo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:46:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T01:18:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm2kl50vkwkdo--58ccec08be88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm2kl50vkwkdo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The AI chip giant reported strong quarterly earnings on Tuesday after the dramatic exit of Jensen Huang.</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe plans to catch the next computer chip wave</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqglwjd450k0o#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:46:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T00:00:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqglwjd450k0o--010b3a1c8069.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqglwjd450k0o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Europe hopes to be a leader in a new generation of computer chips which use light to process data.</summary></entry><entry><title>How new US chip restrictions on South East Asia will hit China</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwq6e2qgvmlgo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:25:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwq6e2qgvmlgo--a126a11490f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwq6e2qgvmlgo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The new rules restrict chip exports and also access to their computing power, which China relies on heavily.</summary></entry><entry><title>NHS data contract to stay with Palantir until 2029</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg27zpm8w8o#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:00:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg27zpm8w8o--2b4aebc65546.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg27zpm8w8o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Despite calls from some Labour MPs to end the arrangement with Palantir, ministers say a new contract will not be awarded until 2029.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pretending to be in New Zealand, booking leave and buying consoles - the lengths fans are going to for GTA 6</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gn9xnn1ppo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:49:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gn9xnn1ppo--55ee5feb0ebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gn9xnn1ppo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Sensor Tower estimates the game has already made $1.18bn from pre-orders across PlayStation and Xbox</summary></entry><entry><title>US government confirms investigation into tech firm Megaspeed</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn504nq5033o#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:17:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn504nq5033o--04b96a357bee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn504nq5033o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Singapore-based company is suspected of helping to ship high-end AI chips from tech giant Nvidia to China, violating US export rules.</summary></entry><entry><title>'We're a capitalist society': Grindr defends $120 a month premium tier</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr1ewlqjn694o#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T09:41:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr1ewlqjn694o--37027c5afa28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr1ewlqjn694o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">It says the ultra-premium service is intended for a "small community" of users - and could get more expensive in future.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia dismisses 'Bring Jensen Back' campaign as Trump backs effort to reinstate ex boss</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cry49plv8v3go#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T02:37:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cry49plv8v3go--4dfe5806c8ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cry49plv8v3go?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">A number of tech figures have backed an effort asking the AI chip giant to give Jensen Huang his job back.</summary></entry><entry><title>The AI start-ups fixing India's broken roads and messy land records</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c820vnln2lzpo#0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T23:25:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c820vnln2lzpo--32ba01daa8e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c820vnln2lzpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">From legal-tech to healthcare, dozens of Indian AI start-ups are solving uniquely Indian challenges.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyw#2</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:47:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyw--1b098827987d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyw?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Video gaming is huge - it's more lucrative than the movies and music combined.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv#2</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv--9798c5d5f4ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">We investigate internet-connected device flaws worldwide, plus US election tech fallout.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt#2</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt--974b9860edd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary ty